# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Anti-Catholicism, part two (group "anticatholic"; 2026-11-26). Freemasonry moved here from "belief": an ideology and a society, not a religion.
# The ideologies and errors that the Church condemned by name (Freemasonry, Communism and socialism, Modernism, Spiritism) are on by default. Each flags what
# PRESENTS, TEACHES, PROMOTES or DEFENDS the thing and spares what warns against it from the Catholic side (a talk, an encyclical, a refutation, a history of the
# persecution); canon 1399 forbids books that defend errors condemned by the Holy See and books that present the Masonic sects as useful and harmless, not books against them.
# The books of the Index of Forbidden Books come "by category". The categories are the rule author's own: the Index is alphabetical and has none. A book rule flags a
# video ABOUT those authors or their works (an analysis, a summary, a reading, an adaptation, a biography, a debate), whatever it says of them: "videos discussing
# these kinds of banned book authors", the rule author, 2026-11-26. The categories that attack the faith directly are on; the broad literary and philosophical
# ones (philosophers, historians, novelists) ship off. Every name and title in their word lists is in docs/en/holy-office/forbidden.md (tests/index-names.test.js).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------

rule communism
  title: Socialism and Communism
  name: Communism and socialism
  plain: Flags content that teaches or praises Communism, Marxism or socialism. Not Catholic warnings against them.
  group: anticatholic
  example: Why communism works: the case for a classless society
  example: Marxism-Leninism explained: the dictatorship of the proletariat
  example: Workers of the world, unite! Join the Communist Party
  spared: Fatima and the errors of Russia: a Catholic talk
  spared: Divini Redemptoris: the Church on atheistic communism
  spared: Priests and nuns who suffered under communism: a documentary
  spared: The Cold War explained: the Soviet Union from 1945 to 1991
  spared: Leninism and Bolshevism @ Apostolic Majesty
  spared: Top Reasons to Oppose Communism @ Ascent of Mount Carmel
  spared: 1. Communist Infiltration of the Catholic Church - Bella Dodd @ Ascent of Mount Carmel
  source: Holy Office decree of 1 July 1949 (AAS 41, p. 334); Syllabus of Errors, section IV (1864); Leo XIII, Quod apostolici muneris (1878); Pius XI, Divini Redemptoris 58 (1937); Catechism 2425. Applying them to videos is a choice of the rule author
  where: feed-card, related, comment, watch-meta
  lexicon: communism_cues, index_socialists
  ask noul: Does this teach, praise or promote Communism, Marxism or socialism (the class struggle, the dictatorship of the proletariat, the Party or the Soviet state) as good or true, and not warn against it from a Catholic viewpoint, tell its history, document its crimes or honour its victims?
  gate: lexicon
  confirm: model
  spare channel: catholic_channels
  flag at: 0.80
  action: feed-card=blank, watch-meta=warn-overlay
  enabled: true

rule modernism
  title: Modernism, the synthesis of all heresies
  name: Modernism
  plain: Flags the Modernist errors that Pius X condemned, such as that dogma evolves. Not Catholic warnings against them.
  group: anticatholic
  example: Dogma evolves: why the Church must change with the times
  example: The Church must change its teaching on contraception
  example: Vital immanence and religious experience: a modern theology
  spared: Pascendi dominici gregis: Pius X on the errors of Modernism
  spared: Newman and the development of doctrine: a Catholic lecture
