  flag at: 0.80
  action: feed-card=blank, watch-meta=warn-overlay
  enabled: true

rule index_freethinkers
  title: Books that attack religion or insult the clergy
  name: Anti-religious writers
  plain: Flags videos about the books and ideas of writers who attacked religion and the clergy and whose books were put on the Index. Not their lives.
  group: anticatholic
  example: Voltaire's Candide: summary and analysis
  example: Baron d'Holbach and the System of Nature: a lecture
  example: Jules Michelet on the priest and the Jesuits: a reading
  spared: Voltaire the French bulldog: our puppy's first week
  spared: Rue Voltaire: a walk through the 11th arrondissement of Paris
  spared: The life of Voltaire: a short biography
  spared: Jules Michelet was born in Paris: his early life
  source: Index of Forbidden Books (1948 and the decrees to 1961), canon 1399, 3 and 6. The categories are a choice of the rule author
  where: feed-card, related, watch-meta
  lexicon: index_freethinkers
  ask noul: Is this video about the books or ideas of writers who attacked religion and the clergy and were put on the Index of Forbidden Books (for example Voltaire, d'Holbach, Michelet or Draper): a reading, a summary, an analysis or an explanation of what they wrote, and not about the life of the person or the history of his time, nor about a place, a school, a street or something else of the same name?
  gate: lexicon
  confirm: model
  spare words: life_words
  flag at: 0.80
  action: feed-card=blank, watch-meta=warn-overlay
  enabled: true

